     "text": "Whether you're selling through an online shop, marketplace, print catalog, or sales app, product information must be accurate, consistent, and available across all channels. For many businesses, this has become a major challenge: product data is spread across multiple systems, processes have evolved over time, and every update requires manual effort. As businesses expand into new sales channels, add more languages, or grow their product portfolios, complexity increases significantly. In addition, today's customers expect complete and reliable product information, regardless of where they interact with your brand. Inaccurate data, inconsistent descriptions, or missing information directly impact the customer experience, conversion rates, and ultimately business success. A Product Information Management (PIM) system provides the foundation to address these challenges. It centralizes product information, standardizes processes, and ensures that every channel accesses the same reliable data source. However, this is where the real challenge begins for many organizations: Which PIM system best fits your business requirements? Choosing a PIM system should not be based solely on features or vendor rankings. The deciding factor is how well the solution aligns with your business processes, existing technology landscape, and long-term strategic goals. Implementing a PIM is not simply a software decision—it is a strategic investment in future-proof commerce and product experience management."
    },
    {
     "role": "body",
     "order": 181,
     "text": "Dorothee Haensch"
